Sensitivity of code E to its input data (noise_tests.py; v1=800, hs=0.2, hv=0.1; max over the rows of |sigma_v - sigma_v(unperturbed)|, v=100 ... 800).
Perturbation: relative 1e-12 of the quantity (constant bias unless marked), applied to the data of the initial row (PROW) or to the horizon column (PCOL).
Reference: the unperturbed run (conv_e.log).  Outcome (note added after Sec. 'The seed of the late-time departure': these perturbations are multiplicative, so they vanish with the field at s=0 and cannot create the additive step in Delta_0 that seeds the late-time growth; see seed_amplitude.log): the response is linear, ~1e-11 to 1e-9 for 1e-12, and does not grow like exp(kappa_+ v) (a growth by 2e10 between v=100 and 800 would be visible).
